                "The fundamental research problem addressed in this study is the pervasive Information-Coordination Asymmetry and Operational Opacity characterizing residential maintenance management in tertiary educational facilities. This problem manifests as a profound disconnect between three primary institutional entities: the student resident who discovers and suffers from physical facility failures, the hall administrative leadership responsible for resource allocation and oversight, and the physical maintenance artisans tasked with executing technical repairs.",
